    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/19/23 12:23:42 PM: David is thinking we are just not making a good connection from top arm to bottom arm. Went back over today and we set tips and arms back up. Welds just fine today. I will monitor, but feel like David was probably right on some small obstruction. | Preston Ellexson - 07/10/23 10:46:33 AM: Inspected welder. No fuses blown. No signs of burning on the main PCB. Reset all to factory parameters and cleared out all functions. Re-programmed schedule in to test with no change. Tried the same with a different, used, board. Same results as above. All welder outputs(1-5) are getting proper voltage. I cycled machine power one by one and tested current on all during a weld sequence. No welder tap settings are producing any current. Awaiting a callback from David @ Spotwelding Consultants to see if we have a bad welder transformer, bad tap switch, or if it's something else.",
