    "completed_datetime": "10/08/2025 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 10/09/25  9:36:19 AM: Mounted a yellow floor post for all 3 of the 120V outlets. Turned breakers off, drilled, anchored, and moved outlets from tables to posts. Turned breakers back on and all outlets are good. Removed all tool holders, air lines, etc from tables. Had operators move their production materials off all tables. Got all 3 tables moved into place. Got outlet strips and brass air lines zip tied to the tables. We didn't drill any holes for anything on any new tables, except tool holders. Added steel safety cable to the shelves on the long tables to support the product weight. These tables are heavy enough they don't need to be anchored. Operators were putting their product back on the tables as we worked on them. Mounted another yellow post in between 2 welders for their flange holder. Everything is completed. I moved the old tables outside maintenance and sent Randy an email on them. Everything is back up and running. | Preston Ellexson - 09/29/25  6:52:45 AM: Forgot I was on vacation Wed-Fri. I am getting a quick game plan together today to give to Randy. I'll get with him and Matt next week when I return to see when we want to complete this. | Preston Ellexson - 09/26/25 11:04:01 AM: Got with Randy and Matt on this. Next week Wed-Fri they have availability for us to get these tables swapped out. I am going to get an eta on Monday. We will have to remount some holders, and remove/replace the brass air line tubing. I'll update Monday after evaluation.",
    "attachments": []
  },
