    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "09/26/2025 11:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 09/29/25  6:51:20 AM: These fuses have plastic fuse holders to remove and install them. They were seating the fuse all the way in the housing. That was causing slight arc flash when the machine was turned on in the mornings. David just removed the holders so you can see the fuses in place. He said he has had a few issues similar and just changed out the fuse block. I don't think this is necessary. I will monitor. | Preston Ellexson - 09/26/25  7:43:47 AM: David will be here shortly to figure out the fuse blowing issue. | Preston Ellexson - 09/23/25  5:35:11 AM: Blew the fuse again this morning. Fuses weren't ordered until yesterday afternoon and won't be here until tomorrow. I locked machine out. David will be here today for the last soft touch install. I'm going to see what he says on the fuse issue. | Preston Ellexson - 09/19/25  5:29:23 AM: A fuse inside the soft touch electrical cabinet was blown. They are very small amperage fuses. I put in one a bit smaller because our next size up was too much of a difference. Machine is running good right now. I sent the correct fuse to be ordered and it says it will be here Tuesday. When it shows up, I'll swap back out to the correct fuse.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "2015",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 2015",
    "equipment_name": "TLE Spotwelder (11816)",
    "department": "Spot Weld",
    "wo_id": "17297",
    "date_notified": "10/15/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "Soft touch blown views",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/David@Spotwelding Consultants",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "10/31/2025 11:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 11/04/25  5:01:19 AM: After David spoke in depth with Untirol, he found the issue. They advised him they accidentally sent fuses sized for 440V not 220V on many of their recent orders. He came and replaced the .3A fuse with 1/2A fuse. Machine hasn't had any issue since. If it happens again, we'll replace the transformer. | Preston Ellexson - 10/27/25  7:56:41 AM: Fuses arrived last week. Welder and soft touch system has been running good since 10/15. No fuses have blown since then. I am still awaiting the transformer from David. | Preston Ellexson - 10/15/25  8:10:22 AM: David is getting with UniControl for a new transformer. | Preston Ellexson - 10/15/25  5:22:35 AM: Replaced fuses with new. Getting with David @ Spotwelding Consultants to order a new transformer and fuse block. If he can't get them soon, we can order them for about $100.",
    "attachments": []
  },
